    "body": "## Summary\n\nBrings **lexbor** (the HTML parser chosen in ADR-001) into the build as a vendored git submodule, embeds it via CMake, and proves it works with a smoke test. This is Phase 0 of the return-to-ADR-001 plan (see ADR-006).\n\nNo integration into `window.cpp` yet — that's Phase 2. This PR is infrastructure-only.\n\n## What's Added\n\n- **`third_party/lexbor`** — git submodule pinned to **v3.0.1** (released 2026-09-07)\n- **Root `CMakeLists.txt`** — embeds lexbor via `add_subdirectory(... EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)` with:\n  - `LEXBOR_BUILD_SHARED=OFF` (we only want the static library)\n  - `LEXBOR_BUILD_STATIC=ON`\n  - Tests, examples, benchmarks, utils, WASM, and install rules all disabled\n- **`tests/CMakeLists.txt`** — links `lexbor_static` into `honeybee_tests`\n- **`tests/test_lexbor_smoke.cpp`** — parses `<html><body><h1>Hello</h1></body></html>`, walks the DOM, asserts the `<h1>` text content. 4 assertions, 1 test case.\n- **`docs/getting-started.md`** — adds `--recursive` to the clone command, explains the submodule, adds a fallback `git submodule update --init --recursive`, and adds a troubleshooting entry for missing `third_party/lexbor`.\n\n## Why Lexbor Ships Its Own CMake\n\nEarlier notes in issue #90 anticipated writing a custom CMake wrapper. That turned out to be unnecessary — lexbor v3 ships a full top-level `CMakeLists.txt` with configurable options. We embed it directly.\n\n## Why Static, Not Shared\n\nStatic keeps `honeybee` self-contained: no `.so` to ship, no `RPATH`/`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` to configure, no risk of loading a different `liblexbor.so` than the one we built. This matches ADR-001's \"vendored\" wording.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuilt and tested locally on Ubuntu 24.04:\n\n```\n$ cmake -S . -B build\n-- Lexbor version: 3.0.1\n-- Append module: core (3.0.1)\n-- Append module: html (2.9.0)\n-- Configuring done\n-- Generating done\n\n$ cmake --build build --target honeybee_tests\n[220/220] Linking CXX executable tests/honeybee_tests\n\n$ ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n1/1 Test #1: honeybee_tests ... Passed  3.06 sec\n100% tests passed, 0 tests failed out of 1\n\n$ ./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[lexbor]\"\nAll tests passed (4 assertions in 1 test case)\n```\n\n## Notes for the Reviewer\n\n- The lexbor build emits many `-Wunused-parameter` warnings from its own code. These are pre-existing in lexbor and not caused by our integration. A future hygiene pass could silence them by adding `-w` to lexbor's target, but that's out of scope here.\n- The first build is slower (~1–2 min) because lexbor compiles ~100 `.c` files. Subsequent incremental builds are fast.\n- Contributors who cloned before this PR will need to run `git submodule update --init --recursive` once.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Builds on Ubuntu 24.04 (CI will confirm)\n- [x] All existing tests pass\n- [x] New smoke test passes\n- [x] Documentation updated\n- [x] No changes to `honeybee` executable behavior\n\nCloses #90\n",
